cases.scenario:
A team needs to add a `timezone` column to their `users` table to support localized notifications. The `users` table currently has 2.5 million rows. Their proposed migration:

```sql
ALTER TABLE users ADD COLUMN timezone VARCHAR(50) DEFAULT 'UTC' NOT NULL;
UPDATE users SET timezone = 'America/New_York' WHERE created_at < '2025-01-01';
```

They plan to run both statements in a single transaction during a maintenance window.
